# {{.Module}}

A TableTheory (Go) quickstart scaffold generated by `tabletheory init --lang go`.

## What's here

- `main.go` — a create/read/update/delete program using TableTheory against DynamoDB Local.
- `dms.yml` — the language-neutral [DMS](https://tabletheory.theorycloud.ai/) description of the `Note` model.
- `docker-compose.yml` — DynamoDB Local (no AWS account required).
- `Makefile` — convenience targets.

## Run it (one command)

```bash
make smoke
```

`make smoke` starts DynamoDB Local and runs the CRUD program. Expected final line:

```
OK: TableTheory CRUD against DynamoDB Local succeeded
```

Equivalently, without make:

```bash
docker compose up -d
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=dummy AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=dummy AWS_REGION=us-east-1 \
  DYNAMODB_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:8000 go run .
```

## Installing the runtime

This scaffold pins `{{.GoModulePath}}`. TableTheory is distributed
through GitHub Releases; update to a specific release with:

```bash
go get {{.GoModulePath}}@{{.GoModuleVersion}}
```

